│ patch_description        │ The current low-parameter candidate (4 distinct params, pure-ZZ ring) scores far below    │
│                          │ the historical best (5 distinct params, with an extra long-range CRZ layer, score 0.52).  │
│                          │ Rather than reintroducing a heavy CRZ hop layer, this edit tests heterogeneous two-qubit  │
│                          │ entanglers as recommended: keep the even/odd RY sublattice rotations (2 params), but      │
│                          │ split the nearest-neighbor entangling ring into two tied-parameter passes — one using     │
│                          │ IsingZZ ("zz") and one using IsingXX ("xx") on the same ring topology — followed by the   │
│                          │ shared final RZ phase layer ("rz_post"). This keeps the same 5 distinct-parameter budget  │
│                          │ as the best-performing candidate while diversifying the type of correlations the circuit  │
│                          │ can build (ZZ commutes with computational-basis features, XX mixes across the X basis),   │
│                          │ which should help generalize a broader range of "hidden difficulty" validation groups     │
│                          │ instead of over-fitting to one entangling axis. Because N_REPEATS=3 already re-applies    │
│                          │ the whole block identically, sequencing ZZ-ring then XX-ring inside one block effectively │
│                          │ realizes an A,B,A,... alternation across repeats without adding extra parameters or       │
│                          │ increasing depth beyond what a single extra ring layer costs.                             │
