                         Patch Metadata - Gen 11/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the best-performing prior candidate (5 distinct parameters: even/odd RY       │
│                          │ rotations, a translation-invariant nearest-neighbor ZZ ring, long-range antipodal CRZ     │
│                          │ couplings, and a globally shared final RZ phase layer, which scored 0.52), this revision  │
│                          │ keeps the exact same parameter budget (5 distinct trainable circuit parameters, 7 total   │
│                          │ with gain/bias) but deepens the entangling structure by adding a second, distance-2 ZZ    │
│                          │ layer that reuses the *same* "zz_ring" parameter name as the nearest-neighbor ring.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale:                                                                                │
│                          │ - The prior ablation showed that collapsing everything into fully-shared single           │
│                          │ parameters (4 distinct params, no even/odd asymmetry) badly hurt accuracy (score dropped  │
│                          │ from 0.52 to 0.36), so the even/odd parity split and the extra long-range coupling are    │
│                          │ essential sources of expressivity that must be preserved.                                 │
│                          │ - The recommendation to deepen the circuit (originally suggested as "increase N_REPEATS") │
│                          │ cannot be applied directly since N_REPEATS is fixed outside the evolve block. Instead, we │
│                          │ deepen the *effective* circuit by adding a second entangling sublayer (distance-2 ZZ      │
│                          │ couplings within each parity class: 0-2-4-6-0 and 1-3-5-7-1) that shares the identical    │
│                          │ "zz_ring" parameter. This adds no new trainable parameters (parameter economy is          │
│                          │ preserved exactly), while giving the ring a richer, next-nearest-neighbor correlation     │
│                          │ structure that should improve the ability to capture harder (worst-group) correlations    │
│                          │ without increasing overfitting risk from added capacity — the extra gates are constrained │
│                          │ to reuse an already-learned angle rather than introducing a new degree of freedom.        │
│                          │ - This mirrors ideas from quantum many-body physics where next-nearest-neighbor couplings │
│                          │ with the *same* coupling constant (translation- and scale-invariant ansatz) provide       │
│                          │ additional entangling power at zero parameter cost, which is exactly the kind of          │
│                          │ structure this problem rewards (parameter economy is weighted very heavily in the score). │
│                          │ - All other structural choices (RY even/odd split, antipodal CRZ, final shared RZ phase   │
│                          │ calibration layer) are kept unchanged since they were empirically validated as important. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps n_distinct_params = 5, n_params = 7 (identical parameter economy to the        │
│                          │ best-known candidate) while giving the ansatz a denser entangling graph that should       │
│                          │ better separate the hardest validation group.                                             │
