                         Patch Metadata - Gen 13/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ revert_to_evenodd_ring_longrange                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The previous edit added a second full entangling ring (an "xx" IsingXX ring on top of the │
│                          │ "zz" IsingZZ ring), which increased depth from 33->54 and param count from 5->5 (same     │
│                          │ count but different topology) yet significantly hurt performance (combined score dropped  │
│                          │ from 0.52 to 0.38). This suggests the extra homogeneous entangling ring adds optimization │
│                          │ difficulty / redundant capacity without adding useful correlations, since the ring        │
│                          │ topology is already covered by "zz" and the readout pairs benefit more from a genuine     │
│                          │ long-range (antipodal) connection than from a second same-topology ring.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit reverts the entangling structure to the empirically best-performing design      │
│                          │ found so far: even/odd RY sublattice rotations (2 params), a single shared ZZ ring (1     │
│                          │ param) matching the ring-like local structure of the readout pairs, a single shared       │
│                          │ long-range CRZ connecting antipodal qubits (1 param) to give every qubit a short path to  │
│                          │ the far side of the register, and a single shared final RZ phase layer (1 param). This    │
