│ patch_description        │ Builds on the strongest prior candidate (even/odd shared RY rotations + shared            │
│                          │ ring/long-range entanglers + shared global RZ phase, which scored 0.52) by restructuring  │
│                          │ the entangling layers so that, together, they cover every pairwise qubit distance         │
│                          │ (1,2,3,4) on the 8-qubit ring — i.e. a complete graph K8 — while still using only two     │
│                          │ distinct entangling parameter names. Distance-1/2 edges share a single IsingZZ parameter  │
│                          │ ("zz_ring") and distance-3/4 edges share a single CRZ parameter ("crz_long"), so the      │
│                          │ trainable parameter count stays the same as the current best (5 distinct circuit          │
│                          │ parameters + 2 readout = 7 total) but the fixed (non-trainable) connectivity is now       │
│                          │ maximal. This exploits the stated principle that "sharing is the only way to reduce       │
│                          │ parameter count without removing gates" in the constructive direction: adding much richer │
│                          │ fixed structure without paying any parameter-count cost. Full all-to-all entanglement,    │
│                          │ replicated across the 3 repeated blocks with tied parameters, should let the small        │
│                          │ parameter budget carve out more robust decision boundaries (better worst-group margin)    │
│                          │ since every readout pair is reachable through short, densely-shared interaction chains    │
│                          │ instead of relying on diffusion around a sparse ring. The even/odd split for local RY     │
│                          │ rotations is kept unchanged since it was empirically the key ingredient that lifted the   │
│                          │ score from ~0.36-0.38 to 0.52.                                                            │
