│ patch_description        │ Revert the ansatz to the higher-scoring even/odd-RY + ZZ-ring + antipodal-CRZ + global-RZ │
│                          │ structure (prior score 0.52), which strongly outperformed the current 3-parameter         │
│                          │ ry/ent/rz variant (score 0.38). On top of that proven base, add a parallel                │
│                          │ nearest-neighbour IsingXX ring sharing a single new parameter "xx_ring", right after the  │
│                          │ ZZ ring. Mixing XX (flip-flop) correlators with the existing ZZ (phase) correlators gives │
│                          │ the entangling layer access to a richer, more expressive two-qubit correlation subspace   │
│                          │ while costing only one extra trainable parameter (6 total instead of 5), which should     │
│                          │ improve worst-group margin/separation without harming the parameter-economy score much,   │
│                          │ and matches the explicit recommendation to test whether orthogonal entanglers boost       │
│                          │ generalization the way the long-range CRZ did.                                            │
