                         Patch Metadata - Gen 17/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ full_connectivity_shared_zz                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current 5-distinct-parameter ansatz (even/odd RY, ZZ ring, antipodal CRZ,     │
│                          │ global RZ) with a minimal 3-distinct-parameter design that outperformed it in prior runs  │
│                          │ (global RY + global RZ + one shared entangling angle), but extend the entangling          │
│                          │ structure from a partial set of shells (distance 1,2,4) to the *complete* graph on 8      │
│                          │ qubits (all pairwise distances 1,2,3,4 covering every one of the 28 edges) using a single │
│                          │ shared IsingZZ angle.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale: the earlier ablation showed that collapsing to 3 shared parameters (global RY, │
│                          │ global RZ, one shared entangler reused across several distance shells) scored             │
│                          │ substantially higher (0.60) than the current 5-parameter even/odd design (0.52),          │
│                          │ confirming that parameter economy dominates the score here. We push this further by       │
│                          │ making the entangling layer fully connected (every qubit pair gets exactly one            │
│                          │ shared-angle interaction) instead of only three shells, which should let correlations     │
│                          │ relevant to *any* dataset-chosen readout pair be captured without adding any new          │
│                          │ trainable parameters (still exactly 3 circuit params + 2 readout params = 5 total). We    │
│                          │ switch CRZ (asymmetric, needs a specific control/target) to the symmetric IsingZZ gate    │
│                          │ for the entangler, since a fully-symmetric interaction should generalize better across    │
│                          │ permutation-like structure in the readout pairs and is consistent with the improved       │
│                          │ generalization seen when moving from asymmetric to shared symmetric operations in the     │
│                          │ prior experiment. This keeps the trainable-parameter count minimal while maximizing the   │
│                          │ diversity/robustness of correlations available to the calibrated readout, targeting       │
│                          │ worst-group margin generalization on held-out difficulty groups.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.1198                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
