                         Patch Metadata - Gen 23/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the strongest prior candidate (global RY + global RZ single-qubit layer,      │
│                          │ followed by a shared-angle CRZ entangler applied across multiple ring "shells", tied      │
│                          │ across all 3 repeated blocks), two key empirical lessons are combined into a new, more    │
│                          │ parameter-frugal design:                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The ablation that diversified entangler axes per shell (CRX/CRY/CRZ) scored *worse*    │
│                          │ than keeping a single CRZ axis everywhere, so axis-uniformity is preserved and even       │
│                          │ reinforced (all entangling gates stay CRZ).                                               │
│                          │ 2. The evolution guidance states parameter count reduction always improves score, with no │
│                          │ diminishing returns, so the two single-qubit rotation angles ("theta_ry", "theta_rz") are │
│                          │ merged into ONE shared parameter "theta1" reused by both the RY and RZ gates on every     │
│                          │ qubit -- this halves the single-qubit-layer parameter count while still producing a       │
│                          │ genuine (non-trivial) fixed-axis single-qubit rotation direction (RZ(theta1)*RY(theta1)), │
│                          │ which becomes richer once composed across the 3 tied repetitions and combined with        │
│                          │ entangling.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To compensate for the reduced single-qubit flexibility, the entangling structure is       │
│                          │ completed into FULL ring connectivity: distances 1, 2, 3, and 4 on the 8-qubit ring       │
│                          │ together cover every one of the 28 possible qubit pairs exactly once, all still driven by │
│                          │ a single shared angle "theta_ent" via CRZ. This gives the circuit maximal                 │
│                          │ correlation-building power between any two qubits (hence any dataset-chosen unknown       │
│                          │ readout pair) while using only 2 distinct circuit parameters (4 total with gain/bias) --  │
│                          │ fewer than every previously tried candidate, aiming to score higher on the                │
│                          │ parameter-economy term while preserving or improving robust worst-group margin through    │
│                          │ denser entanglement.                                                                      │
