│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ revert_to_shell_entangler_plus_final_ry                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The fully-connected ZZ entangler (distance-1,2,3,4, 28 edges) underperformed badly (score │
│                          │ 0.41) compared to the earlier 3-shell CRZ entangler (distance-1,2,4, score 0.60): too     │
│                          │ much entanglement with a single shared angle apparently washes out the signal and hurts   │
│                          │ trainability/generalization. Revert the entangling layer to the proven 3-shell CRZ        │
│                          │ topology (nearest-neighbor ring, skip-2 ring, antipodal pairs) which achieved better      │
│                          │ validation/test accuracy and margin with the same tiny parameter budget. Additionally,    │
│                          │ per the recommendation, append a final global RY layer with a new shared parameter        │
│                          │ "theta_ry_out" after the entangling shells. This acts as a QAOA-style mixer stage that    │
│                          │ can rotate the Bloch vectors into better alignment with the fixed two-qubit readout       │
│                          │ observable after the phase/entangling operations, potentially sharpening class separation │
│                          │ without adding much parameter risk (only +1 param, keeping total distinct params low at   │
│                          │ 4).                                                                                       │
