│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current 5-distinct-parameter even/odd + ZZ-ring + CRZ-long + RZ-all spec              │
│                          │ underperforms (score 0.52) relative to the simpler 2-parameter global-RY + global-RZ +    │
│                          │ 3-shell CRZ-entangler spec (score 0.61) from prior generations. Parameter economy is      │
│                          │ explicitly rewarded ("fewer distinct trainable parameter names ALWAYS scores higher"), so │
│                          │ we revert to that proven 2-parameter backbone (theta_ry for local rotations, theta_z      │
│                          │ shared between the RZ layer and all three CRZ entangling shells — nearest-neighbor, skip, │
│                          │ and antipodal rings on the 8-qubit cycle).                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On top of that proven structure we add a mixer-style closing single-qubit RY layer that   │
│                          │ REUSES the existing "theta_ry" parameter (no new trainable parameter introduced) rather   │
│                          │ than introducing a fresh "theta_ry_out" parameter as the naive QAOA-mixer recommendation  │
│                          │ suggests. This gives the circuit an extra alignment layer after the entangling shells —   │
│                          │ letting the pre-existing rotation angle also act as a final Bloch-vector alignment step   │
│                          │ before measurement — sharpening class separability without paying any parameter-count     │
│                          │ cost. Because parameters are tied across all 3 repeats, this simply changes the           │
│                          │ per-repeat gate sequence (RY-theta_ry, RZ/CRZ-theta_z shells, RY-theta_ry again) while    │
│                          │ keeping N_CIRCUIT_PARAMS at 2, matching the best-performing configuration's economy while │
│                          │ giving optimization one more nonlinear knob to exploit the same 2 parameters, which       │
│                          │ should help robust separation on the hardest validation group and reduce the              │
│                          │ train/validation gap.                                                                     │
