│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ revert_mixer_add_zz_entangler                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The previous edit added a duplicate "mixer-style" RY layer that reuses theta_ry after the │
│                          │ entangling shells. Despite keeping the parameter count at 2, this structural change hurt  │
│                          │ validation/worst-group robustness (score dropped from 0.61 to 0.57), likely because       │
│                          │ doubling the RY layer's effective rotation angle drove qubits further from the sweet spot │
│                          │ needed to align with the fixed two-qubit readout observable, rather than adding useful    │
│                          │ new degrees of freedom.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit reverts that regression: it removes the duplicate closing RY layer, restoring   │
│                          │ the plain 2-parameter (theta_ry, theta_z) structure that scored 0.61. In addition, it     │
│                          │ upgrades the entangling shells from controlled-phase (CRZ) gates to symmetric Ising       │
│                          │ ZZ-type two-qubit rotations (IsingZZ, wired as "ZZ" in the spec) while still sharing the  │
│                          │ same theta_z parameter. CRZ applies an asymmetric conditional phase (it acts differently  │
│                          │ on control vs. target and leaves |0><0| on the control untouched), whereas IsingZZ        │
│                          │ applies a symmetric exp(-i*theta*Z⊗Z/2) rotation to both qubits equally. Since the fixed  │
│                          │ readout is a symmetric two-qubit Hermitian correlator, a symmetric entangling generator   │
│                          │ is a better structural match and should produce cleaner, more consistent two-body         │
│                          │ correlations across the three connectivity shells without adding any new trainable        │
│                          │ parameters, likely improving worst-group margin and validation/test generalization while  │
│                          │ keeping the same minimal parameter count of 2.                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.1005                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
