│ patch_description        │ Building on the best-scoring prior variant (2 distinct circuit parameters: a global       │
│                          │ `theta_ry` local-rotation angle and a global `theta_z` angle shared by both the RZ layer  │
│                          │ and all CRZ entanglers across three connectivity shells — nearest-neighbor, skip, and     │
│                          │ antipodal), this version follows the recommended zero-parameter-growth enrichment: after  │
│                          │ every CRZ edge in all three shells, a matching CRX gate on the SAME wire pair is          │
│                          │ inserted, reusing the identical `theta_z` parameter (no new param names introduced). This │
│                          │ turns each entangling edge from a single Z-Z-type coupling into a combined Z-Z +          │
│                          │ X-mediated coupling (non-commuting rotation axes), giving the ansatz a richer, less       │
│                          │ commutative entangling structure without touching the trainable parameter count (still 2  │
│                          │ distinct circuit params, 4 total with gain/bias). The intuition: since parameter economy  │
│                          │ is rewarded at every step and the current search plateaued at 4 distinct params, forcing  │
│                          │ more expressive multi-axis entanglement while holding parameter count fixed is the most   │
│                          │ direct way to raise the worst-group margin (better boundary shaping) and to shrink the    │
│                          │ train/validation/test gap, since the extra structure comes from architecture, not from    │
│                          │ more free parameters that could overfit the tiny training set.                            │
