╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Builds directly on the best-performing prior seed (global shared RY + RZ rotations with a │
│                          │ triple-shell CRZ entangler reusing theta_rz, which scored 0.61 with only 2 distinct       │
│                          │ circuit parameters) while incorporating the recommended enhancement of adding a single    │
│                          │ shared global RX layer to unlock a third independent local-rotation axis. The previous    │
│                          │ experiment that tried to overload one shared angle across mixed-axis (CRZ+CRX) entangling │
│                          │ gates on the same wire pairs collapsed to chance-level accuracy (0.50) — likely due to a  │
│                          │ destructive symmetry/cancellation between the two axis-different two-qubit gates sharing  │
│                          │ an identical angle on the same pairs across 3 repeated blocks. This design avoids that    │
│                          │ failure mode entirely: entangling gates remain single-axis (CRZ only, reusing theta_rz,   │
│                          │ exactly as in the proven-good seed), and the new RX layer is a purely single-qubit,       │
│                          │ globally-shared addition that cannot interact destructively with the entangler. This      │
│                          │ keeps parameter count economical (3 distinct circuit params + 2 readout = 5 total) while  │
│                          │ giving the state preparation full local SU(2)-like coverage (RX+RY+RZ) before             │
│                          │ entanglement, which should improve worst-group margin and generalization without          │
│                          │ reintroducing the observed instability.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insights:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Proven structure (global RY/RZ + shared CRZ triple-shell entangler) is preserved       │
│                          │ verbatim since it is empirically the best-performing candidate so far.                    │
│                          │ 2. Only ADD to it, never remix axes on the same wires with a shared angle across          │
│                          │ different gate types — that was the root cause of the catastrophic collapse in the        │
│                          │ current program.                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. A single new globally-shared RX parameter cheaply adds a third rotation axis, which    │
│                          │ recommendations flagged as a promising, minimal-risk expressivity boost.                  │
│                          │ 4. Parameter count is kept as low as justified (3 distinct circuit params) to respect the │
│                          │ strong parameter-economy scoring term.                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
