│ patch_name               │ two_param_shell_with_reuse_mixer                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Reverts the failed 3rd-parameter long-range IsingXX shell (which collapsed training       │
│                          │ accuracy to 0.81/0.77) back to the empirically best-performing 2-distinct-parameter       │
│                          │ structure: global RY (theta_ry) + global RZ (theta_z) single-qubit layers, followed by    │
│                          │ two short-range CRZ entangling shells (distance-1 ring and distance-2 skip-ring) that     │
│                          │ reuse theta_z rather than introducing a new entangling parameter. On top of that proven   │
│                          │ backbone, we add a final global RY "mixer" layer that reuses the existing theta_ry        │
│                          │ parameter (no new distinct parameter introduced) after the entangling shells, letting the │
│                          │ circuit rotate the post-entanglement Bloch vectors into better alignment with the fixed   │
│                          │ two-qubit readout observable. This keeps n_distinct_params at 2 (matching the             │
│                          │ highest-scoring prior candidate, 0.61) while adding extra expressivity for readout        │
│                          │ alignment, which should help both average and worst-group margins without any             │
│                          │ parameter-count penalty.                                                                  │
