│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_axis_entangler_theta_z_crx                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Revert to the empirically superior 2-parameter local-rotation scheme (independent         │
│                          │ theta_ry for a global RY layer and theta_z for a global RZ layer, score 0.61) rather than │
│                          │ the theta_su-merged variant that regressed to 0.58 by collapsing per-qubit RY+RZ into one │
│                          │ angle (losing per-qubit two-axis expressivity). On top of that proven base, enrich the    │
│                          │ entangling shells by inserting a CRX gate for every pair that already has a CRZ gate,     │
│                          │ reusing the SAME theta_z parameter (non-commuting X-axis controlled rotation added at     │
│                          │ zero extra parameter cost). This tests whether adding an orthogonal-axis entangling       │
│                          │ pathway (CRZ + CRX sharing one angle) improves worst-group margin/generalization without  │
│                          │ increasing the parameter budget beyond 2 circuit parameters (4 total with gain/bias),     │
│                          │ which the scoring rule rewards unconditionally.                                           │
