│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ remove_output_mixer_reuse                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate added a final global RY layer that reuses "theta_ry" as a           │
│                          │ post-entangling "output mixer" at zero extra parameter cost. Empirically this hurt        │
│                          │ performance: the current program scores 0.57 (validation accuracy 0.88) versus the        │
│                          │ earlier 2-parameter multi-shell candidate without this mixer layer, which scored 0.61     │
│                          │ (validation accuracy 0.90). Reusing theta_ry for both the initial state-preparation       │
│                          │ rotation and a final pre-measurement rotation couples two roles that want different       │
│                          │ optimal angles under gradient descent, since the parameter is shared identically across   │
│                          │ all 3 repeated blocks and now also across both intra-block sub-roles -- this likely       │
│                          │ creates conflicting gradients that slow/impair convergence (worst_group_margin also       │
│                          │ dropped from 0.35/0.33 baseline). Removing the redundant output-mixer layer reverts to    │
│                          │ the simpler, empirically stronger 2-parameter structure (theta_ry local rotation +        │
│                          │ theta_z shared across RZ layer and all three CRZ entangling shells), restoring the higher │
│                          │ validation accuracy and margin while keeping the same minimal parameter count.            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
