│ patch_description        │ The current ANSATZ_SPEC added a final global RY "output mixer" layer that reuses the      │
│                          │ existing theta_ry parameter at (nominally) zero extra parameter cost. However,            │
│                          │ empirically this hurt performance significantly: validation accuracy dropped from 0.90 to │
│                          │ 0.88, and worse, the run never reached the convergence threshold within the training      │
│                          │ budget (convergence_step_mean: None vs 1440 previously), and the combined score dropped   │
│                          │ from 0.61 to 0.57. The extra RY layer right before every repeated block's next RY layer   │
│                          │ effectively just shifts the phase of the following rotation, adding optimization          │
│                          │ difficulty (interacting with the entangling CRZ layers across repeats) without adding     │
│                          │ real expressive power, since parameters are tied across all 3 repeats. Removing it        │
│                          │ restores the simpler, better-converging 2-parameter design (global RY, global RZ reused   │
│                          │ as CRZ angle across 3 entangling shells) that previously achieved the best combined score │
│                          │ (0.61) with only 2 distinct trainable circuit parameters, better validation accuracy, and │
│                          │ reliable convergence.                                                                     │
