│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current 5-parameter ansatz (ry_even/ry_odd/zz_ring/crz_long/rz_all, which     │
│                          │ scored only 0.52) with a restructured version of the best-performing prior candidate (2   │
│                          │ distinct params: theta_ry, theta_z; score 0.61). Per the evolution guidance that fewer    │
│                          │ distinct parameter names always score higher, and per the specific recommendation to      │
│                          │ interleave the RZ layer between entangling shells rather than applying all rotations      │
│                          │ before or after the entangling shells in one block, this candidate:                       │
│                          │ 1) Drops back to exactly 2 distinct trainable circuit parameters (theta_ry, theta_z) plus │
│                          │ gain/bias (4 total), which was empirically both higher-scoring and had a smaller          │
│                          │ train/validation loss than the 4-5 parameter variants tried so far.                       │
│                          │ 2) Keeps the rich 3-shell CRZ entangling graph (distance 1, 2, 4 rings) that gives        │
│                          │ near-complete qubit connectivity with tied parameters.                                    │
│                          │ 3) Moves the global RZ layer (reusing theta_z) from before all entangling shells to       │
│                          │ between Shell 1 (nearest-neighbor ring) and Shell 2 (skip ring), so that within one block │
│                          │ the sequence is RY -> Shell1 -> RZ -> Shell2 -> Shell3. This gives an extra local-phase   │
│                          │ mixing point between entangling stages, which combined with 3x block repetition, should   │
│                          │ improve gradient propagation and worst-case margin without increasing the parameter       │
│                          │ count.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This directly follows both hard constraints (parameter economy dominates score) and the   │
│                          │ qualitative recommendation about interleaving rotation layers between entangling shells.  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
