                         Patch Metadata - Gen 51/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Structural refinement of the best-performing 2-parameter seed (global shared RY + RZ      │
│                          │ single-qubit layers with a shared-angle CRZ entangling network). Instead of driving every │
│                          │ entangling shell with the same rotation axis as before, this version diversifies the      │
│                          │ *entangling gate axis per shell* while still reusing only the two existing single-qubit   │
│                          │ parameter names — no new trainable circuit parameters are introduced. Specifically:       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Global RY(theta_ry) and RZ(theta_z) layers on all 8 qubits (unchanged).                 │
│                          │ - Shell 1 (nearest-neighbor ring, distance 1): CRZ gates reusing theta_z — same axis as   │
│                          │ the RZ layer, proven safe and effective.                                                  │
│                          │ - Shell 2 (skip ring, distance 2): CRY gates reusing theta_ry — a *new* cross-axis        │
│                          │ entangling shell that couples qubits through the Y generator instead of Z, using the      │
│                          │ existing theta_ry parameter. This increases the diversity of correlations the circuit can │
│                          │ build (mixing Y- and Z-type two-qubit couplings) without adding any new distinct          │
│                          │ parameter names, and crucially avoids the destructive failure mode observed when the same │
│                          │ shared angle drives two conflicting generators (CRZ+CRX) *on the same wire pairs* — here  │
│                          │ the cross-axis shell acts on a disjoint set of pairs from the same-axis shell.            │
│                          │ - Shell 3 (antipodal ring, distance 4): CRZ gates reusing theta_z, matching the           │
│                          │ long-range topology of the previous best seed.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Total gate count per block (36) and total repeated-block gate count (108) exactly match   │
│                          │ the earlier 0.61-scoring seed, so circuit depth and optimizer step cost are unchanged,    │
│                          │ but the entangling structure now spans two rotation axes instead of one, which should     │
│                          │ improve the network's ability to correlate hard-to-separate validation groups (better     │
│                          │ worst-group margin) while keeping parameter economy (2 distinct circuit parameters, 4     │
│                          │ total trainable scalars) that the evolution history shows is strongly rewarded.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a pure architectural reshuffle of the EVOLVE-BLOCK content: no changes to the     │
│                          │ fixed training loop, dataset handling, measurement, or block-repetition logic.            │
