│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ antipodal_cry_shared_theta_z                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Revert to the higher-scoring 3-shell shared-CRZ backbone (nearest-neighbor, skip,         │
│                          │ antipodal rings, all keyed to theta_z, plus a shared theta_ry local layer) that           │
│                          │ previously achieved combined score 0.61, dropping the final-RY-mixer variant that         │
│                          │ regressed to 0.55. On top of that proven backbone, apply the targeted axis-mixing         │
│                          │ recommendation: in Shell 3 (the four antipodal, distance-4 pairs) swap CRZ for CRY while  │
│                          │ still reusing the same shared "theta_z" parameter name (so the parameter count stays at 2 │
│                          │ distinct circuit parameters). Rationale: CRZ commutes with the RZ single-qubit layer and  │
│                          │ with the CRZ gates in shells 1/2, so all Z-generated rotations only ever dephase relative │
│                          │ phases and never rotate Bloch vectors out of the Z-eigenbasis structure imposed by the    │
│                          │ local RZ layer -- this leaves a residual symmetry (global relative-phase invariance) that │
│                          │ a state's Z-basis populations alone cannot break. Introducing a Y-axis controlled         │
│                          │ rotation only on the long-range antipodal links forces those particular qubit pairs to    │
│                          │ develop entanglement that is not diagonal in the same basis as the rest of the circuit,   │
│                          │ which should let the read-out observable pick up a genuinely different (non-commuting)    │
│                          │ correlation structure specifically from the hardest, most long-range-correlated           │
│                          │ validation examples, without adding any new trainable parameter.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0923                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 6; deleted: 0; modified: 24;                                                       │
