│ patch_description        │ The current ANSATZ_SPEC (2-shell design + appended theta_ry mixer reusing the RY          │
│                          │ parameter) regressed performance to 0.55 combined score, well below the previously        │
│                          │ validated 3-shell design (distance-1, distance-2, distance-4 CRZ shells all sharing       │
│                          │ "theta_z", with no post-entanglement RY mixer) which achieved 0.61. The extra final RY    │
│                          │ layer apparently interferes with the more limited 2-shell entangling structure, dropping  │
│                          │ train accuracy from 1.00 to 0.75. This edit reverts to the empirically superior 3-shell   │
│                          │ backbone (still only 2 distinct circuit parameters: theta_ry, theta_z) as the base to     │
│                          │ build further improvements from, since parameter count and structure quality both matter  │
│                          │ and this is the strongest known 2-parameter configuration.                                │
