│ patch_name               │ rz_output_mixer                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate appends a closing RY layer that reuses "theta_ry" after the         │
│                          │ CRZ-dominated entangling shells, but this scored worse (0.57) than the prior seed without │
│                          │ that closing mixer (0.61). The entangling shells and the CRZ layer operate in the RZ      │
│                          │ (Z-axis) basis, so a closing rotation axis mismatched from that basis (RY) may be         │
│                          │ fighting the alignment the entangler already built up, rather than aiding the Hermitian   │
│                          │ readout alignment. Replace the closing RY("theta_ry") layer with a closing RZ("theta_z")  │
│                          │ layer instead: this keeps the rotation axis consistent with the CRZ-based entangling      │
│                          │ shells, giving the optimizer one more use of the already-shared "theta_z" parameter to    │
│                          │ fine-tune phase alignment before readout, at zero extra parameter cost (still 2 distinct  │
│                          │ circuit params). This directly tests the axis-alignment hypothesis from the               │
│                          │ recommendation while preserving the low parameter count that dominates the score.         │
