│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ single_shared_param_ansatz                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Collapse the two distinct trainable circuit parameters ("theta_ry" and "theta_z") into a  │
│                          │ single shared parameter name "theta" used for both the local RY/RZ rotations and all CRZ  │
│                          │ entangling shells. Parameter economy is explicitly the dominant scoring factor with "no   │
│                          │ point of diminishing returns," so going from 2 to 1 distinct circuit parameters (3 total  │
│                          │ trainable values with gain/bias) should improve the score even at some accuracy cost. The │
│                          │ circuit retains its full gate structure (same three entangling shells, same interleaved   │
│                          │ RZ layer) — only the parameter name binding changes, so expressivity through gate         │
│                          │ placement, wire connectivity, and 3x repetition is preserved; only the number of          │
│                          │ independently-optimizable scalars shrinks. This also reduces train/test gap risk since    │
│                          │ fewer parameters constrain overfitting on the very small training set, aligning with the  │
│                          │ goal of robust worst-group generalization.                                                │
