│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shell3_boost_no_mixer                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Reverts the previous output-mixer addition (which regressed score from 0.61 to 0.57 by    │
│                          │ adding a redundant final RY layer that interfered with the readout alignment) and instead │
│                          │ applies the recommended idea of softly breaking symmetry between entangling shells at     │
│                          │ zero parameter cost. Since apply_ansatz_block (outside the evolve block) does not support │
│                          │ arbitrary scale factors, we achieve an equivalent, schema-legal multiplier by repeating   │
│                          │ the CRZ gate on each distance-4 (antipodal) edge twice. Two consecutive CRZ(theta_z)      │
│                          │ applications on the same wire pair compose additively into a single effective             │
│                          │ CRZ(2*theta_z) rotation, giving the long-range antipodal shell double the effective       │
│                          │ coupling strength relative to the nearest-neighbor and skip shells -- directionally       │
│                          │ matching the recommendation to boost the far-shell coupling -- while preserving full      │
│                          │ rotational symmetry within each shell (all edges in a shell still get identical           │
│                          │ treatment), which prior logged experiments showed is critical: anisotropic/asymmetric     │
│                          │ treatment within a shell collapsed training. This keeps the 2-distinct-parameter economy  │
│                          │ (theta_ry, theta_z) that scored best while diversifying the effective entangling          │
│                          │ structure.                                                                                │
