│ patch_name               │ final_rz_mixer_theta_z                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Add a final shared-parameter RZ mixer layer (reusing "theta_z") on all 8 qubits after the │
│                          │ three entangling CRZ shells. Since the entangling layer is itself CRZ-based (also using   │
│                          │ theta_z), a trailing local RZ layer on the same axis lets the circuit re-align            │
│                          │ single-qubit phases picked up during entanglement before the next repetition/readout,     │
│                          │ without adding any new trainable parameter (still 2 distinct circuit params). This tests  │
│                          │ whether an axis-consistent closing rotation improves the worst-group margin and           │
│                          │ convergence speed relative to leaving the block ending on the antipodal CRZ shell.        │
